{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2"],"primary":"c2","title":"Santa Ana Rent Stabilization and Just Cause Eviction Ordinance - just cause eviction and relocation assistance","requirement":"After 30 days of tenancy, an owner may not end a tenancy without a just cause (at-fault, such as unpaid rent, a material lease breach, nuisance or criminal activity; or no-fault, such as owner move-in, withdrawal from the rental market, or demolition or substantial remodel), and the cause must be stated in a written notice, with an opportunity to cure required before an at-fault termination. For no-fault terminations, the owner must provide 3 months' relocation assistance or waive the final 3 months' rent.","key_value":"Just cause required after 30 days of tenancy; no-fault termination requires 3 months' relocation assistance or 3 months' rent waiver","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2021-11-19","end_date":null,"citation":"Santa Ana Rent Stabilization and Just Cause Eviction Ordinance","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental tenancies in Santa Ana that have lasted more than 30 days.","exemptions":"Housing produced in the last 15 years; deed-restricted affordable housing; hotel and transient occupancy; hospital and care facilities; dormitories; and other shared living quarters.","coverage_from":"c2","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
